 "notes": "2026-27 is the third season of the 2024-29 domestic cycle (DAZN all 380 matches, 10 per round with 7 exclusive; Sky 3 per round co-exclusive = 114) and the last season of the 2024-27 international cycle in most territories. Lega Serie A sells most territories directly; Infront manages 36 APAC territories for 2024-25 to 2026-27. The official Lega Serie A broadcasters page (en.legaseriea.it/serie-a/broadcasters, titled 2025/26) only shows Italy (DAZN, Sky); there is no official worldwide list online. Most international entries therefore come from Wikipedia's 'List of Serie A broadcasters' (an undated table that looks current for 2026-27, since it already includes Telemundo and the BBC). Entries verified by 2026 news are UK, Ireland, US, France, Germany, Austria, Switzerland and Pakistan; the rest are flagged as not independently confirmed. In Italy there is no live free-to-air Serie A. Rai and Mediaset hold only free-to-air highlights, and DAZN may stream up to five matches free. A few SE Asian/Central Asian entries come only from the Wikipedia 'Serie A' article's 2024-29 section and may be stale. FTA flags for some smaller satellite or state channels are inferred from the channel's normal distribution model, as noted per entry.",
